WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.540
So what does community mean to you?

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.960
When you look at a community, Sasol, Conoco is a part of this community.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.780
A very important part of this community.

4
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.040
Without them there probably wouldn’t be a community.

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.100
Because, you know, jobs are important.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.920
I mean I worked at . . . for L&amp;G plant, you know.

7
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.980
So if you don’t have jobs, you don’t have the means for a person to make a living then.

8
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:32.100
But there got to be that medium where everybody can be satisfied.

9
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.340
And that’s what I think.

10
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.680
I’m not against all this.

11
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.840
I’m not against it.

12
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.980
But it’s a sadness anytime you lose something.

13
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:46.220
The most important thing I want people to remember is that when you drive down Old Spanish Trail,

14
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:55.640
you may . . . This community center may still be here, the swimming pool and all that, but there were people here, too.

15
00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.640
A lot of African American people were here.

16
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:06.780
And I think this is one of the communities that survived after slavery after . . . during Reconstruction and all that.

17
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:13.620
It didn’t grow as big as some of the other communities, but they were here, you know.

18
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:18.320
And one of these days, when you drive down here, you’re going to see a fence.

19
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.780
An eight foot fence with that wire, that razor wire all around it.

20
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:26.200
But at one time they had people living there.

21
00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.480
And that’s not a bad thing I don’t think.

22
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.320
I’m not trying to say it’s a bad thing, but it is what it is.

23
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:42.660
And hopefully that some of these jobs that they bringing in will trickle down to some of the people living in this area.

24
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:50.120
Because one thing that I’ve noticed . . . I’m not trying to point no finger at nobody, I don’t know why,

25
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:58.680
but a lot of times when economic boom happens, it don’t necessarily happen for the people that it affect the most.

26
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.560
And that’s the sadness that I see in it.

27
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:08.940
Now it may be because that person didn’t assert his self to get that job or whatever,

28
00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:14.760
but that’s the only thing that I pray that we all prosper from this.

29
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.360
Not just a select few.
